{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule0aB0V","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdjacencyList"}],"modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AdjacencyList","remoteSource":{"fileName":"AdjacencyList.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList.swift#L24"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"}]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s17CustomReflectableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/Se","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SE","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SH","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Neighbors"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init()","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(_:)-2unw2","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(_:)-6cbnw","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(adjacency:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(edges:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(vertices:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(vertices:edges:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/insert(edge:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomDebugStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomReflectable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Decodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Encodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteral-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Hashable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/MutableDirectedGraph-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdjacencyList"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertex set is any set of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a weight can live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in an array beside the graph. Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row of those edges’ positions, and a row of its in-neighbors; the rows of each kind share one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(amortized, like ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and copying it copies a constant number of buffers. A hash table from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slot pair to position (open addressing with a multiplicative hash, not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Dictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s SipHash)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answers ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in O(1) expected. A graph built in bulk from sorted edges (a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"condensation, a line graph, a named graph) builds that table on its first lookup or mutation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in O(m), so a result that is only traversed never pays for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/adjacencylist"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph stored as out- and in-adjacency lists."}],"references":{"doc://AdjacencyListModule/doc